
<p>Ryan Christoffel, 9to5Mac:</p>

<blockquote>
  <p>Apple confirmed to 9to5Mac that the ads rollout in Maps began in
the last few days. And it will continue ramping in the weeks ahead
to all users.</p>

<p>There are two places you’ll find ads in the Maps app:</p>

<ol>
<li>Before searching: Suggested Places in the search screen will
feature an ad.</li>
<li>After searching: Ads will appear in search results when
relevant.</li>
</ol>
</blockquote>

<p>Before searching, I saw an ad for an HVAC contractor 12 miles away in “Suggested Places”. Knock on wood but I currently have no HVAC problems, and even if I did, I’d just call someone and have them come here. Then I waited a few minutes and looked again. This time I <a href="https://daringfireball.net/misc/2026/08/tommys-express-carwash.jpeg">saw an ad</a> for Tommy’s Express Car Wash (“Get your first month free”), 23 miles away in the middle of a suburban shopping mall. Apple Maps estimates it would take me 1 hour 8 minutes to drive there right now. I’ll get right on that.</p>

<p>The first organic (non-ad) suggested place is a coffee shop 300 feet away.</p>

